    <!-- A Super 32X game with one sound driver, a Z80 program in the cartridge (0x2000 in the file; the game's 68000 copies it to the Z80's RAM). It plays
         the Z80 side's effects on the YM2612 and the PSG and, for the music, writes events for a synthesizer that runs on the slave SH-2 and plays through the
         PWM unit: a ring buffer in the Z80's RAM (the write index at 0x16FF, the events from 0x1700). The game's 68000 takes the events out and hands each to the slave through
         the communication words; here the Machine does that (sh2_event_ring). The 68000 writes a request into the driver's request bytes at 0x16F0
         (0x80 when free). The Z80 reads the cartridge through the 32X windows (cart_window). -->
